<title>FRANCE: France to create 40,000 to 70,000 jobs for young.</title>
<headline>France to create 40,000 to 70,000 jobs for young.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-07-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>The French government plans to create 40,000 to 70,000 public sector jobs for young people this year, at a cost of some two billion francs, Finance Minister Dominique Strauss-Kahn said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Many of the jobs would be in education, he told a news conference.</p>
<p>&quot;It represents several tens of thousands of jobs...at least 40,000 to 50,000 and at most 60,000 to 70,000,&quot; he said.</p>
<p>He said the exact number of jobs created and the cost depended on how quickly young people could be hired.</p>
</text>
